# FUNCTION VAR is not retained between calls.
#
# Derivation: ed.3 6.6.2.1 (ed.2 2.5.1): a function has no internal state,
# so an invocation with the same arguments yields the same result; its VAR
# variables are initialised at each invocation. Hence f = x on every
# cycle; a retained n would give the running sum instead (3, 7, 7, 2).
period_ms: 100
program: main
inputs: x
outputs: f
status: conformant
reference: IEC 61131-3 ed.3 6.6.2.1 (functions have no internal state)
---
0 x=3  => f=3
1 x=4  => f=4
2 x=0  => f=0
3 x=-5 => f=-5
